{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Please, Adonai, send, etc.</b> That is, I am not — heaven forbid — attributing the impediment to the Creator, for He is omnipotent; rather, the inability to remove the blemish stems from my side, for I am unworthy of a miracle. And His saying ״please, Adonai״ suspends upon Himself the entire deficiency and hindrance. And His saying <b>send, please</b>, etc. — meaning, by the hand of one who is worthy to perform Your mission, not through one as lowly as me in whom my blemish is fixed. And this declares my being unfit for so exalted a mission:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:27.846444457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}